  "title": "Urethroplasty",
  "description": "Urethroplasty repairs damage or narrowing of the urethra caused by stricture, injury, or birth defects. Treatment approaches range from simple widening procedures to complex reconstruction with grafts or flaps. Your urologist assesses the stricture location and extent to determine the best surgical approach. Success rates are high with modern techniques, and most patients experience restored normal urinary flow and elimination of symptoms.",
